َدِيرٌۭ","t":"All-Powerful","p":"N","tr":"qadīrun","f":["M","INDEF","NOM"],"r":81,"l":260},{"e":"٥٠","v":"30:50"}]}],"verses":[{"k":"30:42","t":"Say, [O Muḥammad], \"Travel through the land and observe how was the end of those before. Most of them were associators [of others with Allāh].","j":21,"h":41,"s":30,"a":42,"sd":null},{"k":"30:43","t":"So direct your face [i.e., self] toward the correct religion before a Day comes from Allāh of which there is no repelling. That Day, they will be divided.","j":21,"h":41,"s":30,"a":43,"sd":null},{"k":"30:44","t":"Whoever disbelieves - upon him is [the consequence of] his disbelief. And whoever does righteousness - they are for themselves preparing,","j":21,"h":41,"s":30,"a":44,"sd":null},{"k":"30:45","t":"That He may reward those who have believed and done righteous deeds out of His bounty. Indeed, He does not like the disbelievers.","j":21,"h":41,"s":30,"a":45,"sd":null},{"k":"30:46","t":"And of His signs is that He sends the winds as bringers of good tidings and to let you taste His mercy [i.e., rain] and so the ships may sail at His command and so you may seek of His bounty, and perhaps you will be grateful.","j":21,"h":41,"s":30,"a":46,"sd":null},{"k":"30:47","t":"And We have already sent messengers before you to their peoples, and they came to them with clear evidences; then We took retribution from those who committed crimes, and incumbent upon Us was support of the believers.","j":21,"h":41,"s":30,"a":47,"sd":null},{"k":"30:48","t":"It is Allāh who sends the winds, and they stir the clouds and spread them in the sky however He wills, and He makes them fragments so you see the rain emerge from within them. And when He causes it to fall upon whom He wills of His servants, immediately they rejoice","j":21,"h":41,"s":30,"a":48,"sd":null},{"k":"30:49","t":"Although they were, before it was sent down upon them - before that, in despair.","j":21,"h":41,"s":30,"a":49,"sd":null},{"k":"30:50","t":"So observe the effects of the mercy of Allāh - how He gives life to the earth after its lifelessness. Indeed, that [same one] will give life to the dead, and He is over all things competent.","j":21,"h":41,"s":30,"a":50,"sd":null}],"juz":21,"hizb":41,"surahs":[30],"sajdah":false}